   best_p = initial_p\n            best_corr = evaluate_objective(best_p)\n\n            candidate_pool = resample_uniformly(best_p, n_points=5)\n\n            last_update = time.time()\n            iteration = 0\n            max_iterations = 1000   # until time out\n\n            while time.time() - start < max_time and iteration < max_iterations:\n                for candidate in candidate_pool:\n                    new_corr = evaluate_objective(candidate)\n                    if new_corr < best_corr:\n                        best_corr = new_corr\n                        best_p = candidate.copy()\n                        \n                    candidate_pool = replace_worst_candidate(candidate_pool, best_p)\n                    \n                if time.time() - last_update > 60 or update_counter(10):\n                    # Update candidate pool and grid resolution\n                    ...\n                    \n                iteration += 1\n                \n            return best_p, best_corr, len(best_p)\n\n   5. **Search Choices**\n        a. Resolution Selection:\n            Start at current grid size, increase by 20% when:\n            - Progress stalls for 10 updates\n            - Correlation floor below 0.375 is consistent for 3 measurements\n            \n        b. Adaptation Rules:\n            - Exploration Phase: Crossover probabilities (0.7 local search, 0.3 global)\n            - Exploitation Phase: Crossover probabilities (0.3 local search)\n            - Switch rule: Based on observed improvement rates\n\n   6. **Budget and Overhead**\n        - Estimation: Principal cost is FFT-based correlation evaluation, O(n log n)\n        - Initial resources: ~800 seconds on 1 core for response surface exploration\n        - Final polish: Constrained gradient optimization on final candidate\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**\n   - Core Strategy:\n     1. Basis Adaptation:\n        - **Basis Expansion**: Gradually replace basis functions as grid expands\n        - **Basis Weakening**: Reduce influence of distant grid points\n        - **Direction Change**: When progress stalls, abandon current solution\n\n     2. Probabilistic Selection:\n        - Crossover mix: main loop -> 70% local, 30% global\n        - Candidate selection: Replace 25% of worst performing periodically\n\n     3. Hyperparameter Sweeps:\n        - Time budget: 50% exploration, 50% refinement\n        - Weight evolution: Increase from 0.05 to 0.2 in 10 steps\n\n     4. Termination Clauses:\n        - Plateau detection: 20 evaluations with no improvement\n        - Progress decay: Improvement rate <0.05 quad/iteration\n        - Time out for individual evaluations\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**\n   - Dominant cost: correlation computation across 2n-1 shifts\n   - Implementation: Use FFT-based cross correlation via numpy's correlate\n   - Memory: Current fit requires ~1600 points without extraordinary features\n   - Time allocation: 0-30% for basis expansion, 70% for detailed local search\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n   - Feasibility checkpoints before each return:\n     1. Integral check: |\u222bhdx - 0.5| < 1e-5\n     2. Boundary check: min(h,g) >= 0\n     3. Outlier detection in correlations\n   - Evaluation re-calculation for final solution\n   - Full objective evaluation: C = (Hankel matrix of correlations) * dx_max\n\n   Return format: (numpy_array_h, final_C, grid_size)",
